EduDFS is an independent teaching project. Its design, terminology and
class, method and field names are inspired by Apache Hadoop HDFS so that
learners can find the corresponding code in the original project. It
contains no source code from Apache Hadoop.

EduDFSBase (package edudfsbase) is part of this project. Its design,
terminology and names are inspired by Apache HBase in the same way. It
contains no source code from Apache HBase.

In both parts, class, method, field and configuration names, file
layouts, magic strings, shell syntax and some short log and error
messages deliberately follow the originals, so that learners recognize
them. The MurmurHash2 function (edudfsbase.util.MurmurHash) implements
the public-domain algorithm by Austin Appleby; its Java formulation
follows the common Java port also found in Apache Hadoop and Apache
HBase (Apache License 2.0).

